Keep DMARC aggregate reporting working on alpine 3.22. That release builds rspamd against Lua 5.4 rather than LuaJIT, which turns a latent bug in rspamd's `dmarc.lua` into a fatal one: report data silently stops reaching redis while DMARC policy evaluation keeps working, so nothing looks broken. Until a fixed rspamd reaches alpine, the rspamd image patches the packaged plugin during the build. The patch is self-limiting -- the build fails once the shipped file already contains the fix, which is the signal to delete the `RUN` block in `core/rspamd/Dockerfile` and nothing else.
